Common Issues Faced When Setting Up Selenium Java Scripts from Scratch

🔧 1. Environment & Dependency Issues
Issue	Root Cause	Solution
WebDriver class not found	Selenium JARs not added	Use Maven with proper pom.xml
Browser driver not recognized	Missing ChromeDriver/GeckoDriver	Use WebDriverManager to handle it automatically
Incompatible driver/browser versions	ChromeDriver vs Chrome version mismatch	Use latest compatible versions OR WebDriverManager
Java version issues	Using unsupported JDK version for a lib	Stick with JDK 8–17 depending on library support
Build issues	Incorrect or missing Maven config	Reimport Maven project / check pom.xml for errors

🧪 2. Web Element Interaction Issues
Issue	Root Cause	Solution
ElementNotInteractableException	Element not visible or not loaded yet	Use explicit waits (WebDriverWait)
NoSuchElementException	Incorrect or dynamic locator	Validate locator in browser dev tools and use relative XPath/CSS
Elements in iframe	Trying to access an element inside an iframe	Use driver.switchTo().frame() before interacting
Pop-ups or alerts	Alert window blocks interaction	Handle with driver.switchTo().alert()
Multiple windows/tabs	Trying to interact without switching	Use getWindowHandles() to switch to correct tab/window

⏳ 3. Timing & Synchronization Issues
Issue	Root Cause	Solution
Script runs too fast	Page elements not loaded	Add explicit waits (best) or Thread.sleep() (temporary)
StaleElementReferenceException	DOM updated, element reference lost	Re-locate the element right before action
Asynchronous JS elements	Modern web apps (React, Angular) load dynamically	Use conditions like elementToBeClickable, presenceOfElementLocated, etc.

🗃️ 4. Framework-Level Design Issues
Issue	Root Cause	Solution
Hard-coded values	URL, credentials, locators in script	Externalize using config.properties, data files, environment variables
Unstructured code	No separation of logic and test	Use Page Object Model (POM) for maintainability
No reusability	Repeated code for browser setup, teardown	Use utility classes or test base class
Test execution is manual	No test runner integrated	Use TestNG or JUnit for test execution & grouping

📊 5. Reporting & Logging Issues
Issue	Root Cause	Solution
No test result visibility	Just using System.out.println	Integrate ExtentReports / Allure Reports
Hard to debug failures	No logs	Use Log4j or SLF4J for proper logging
Screenshots missing	Not capturing on failure	Add screenshot capture in @AfterMethod or test failure hooks

🔁 6. Continuous Integration (CI/CD) Issues
Issue	Root Cause	Solution
Script works locally but fails in Jenkins	Environment differences	Use headless mode or configure Jenkins agent properly
Driver not found in CI/CD	Path issues	Use WebDriverManager or set drivers in pipeline config
Flaky tests	Timing or test dependencies	Use retry logic, proper waits, and keep tests isolated

📦 7. Real-Time Project Issues
Problem	Solution
Business logic changes frequently	Keep locators and logic loosely coupled via Page Object Model
DOM elements have dynamic IDs	Use XPath functions like contains(), starts-with()
Parallel execution needed	Use TestNG + ThreadLocal WebDriver or Selenium Grid
Need to test across browsers	Use @Parameters to handle cross-browser testing

✅ Pro Tips:
	• Start simple, and gradually modularize the framework.
	• Keep reusable code in utility/helper classes.
	• Use BaseTest class for setup/teardown methods.
	• Externalize test data and configs.
	• Use Git to version control your framework.
	• Build scripts to clean and build the project automatically.

